I+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"5053c20eea0f3502b04d874314eab57baafc3823e86c67af7e410e018b75b3e7","event_uuid":"fba4eb91-3a6a-4bc4-b2a3-5ffa56a058cb","position":{"commit_sha":"05ad07b62c1034ac1173281c3d9bff5a8b028ce8","position":"1795153204107015001-fba4eb91-3a6a-4bc4-b2a3-5ffa56a058cb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Approach changed before any review completed: the coordinator ruled out skipping or deselecting the test. The test now uses a key that is invalid on every platform, plus a binding-level test that pins the per-platform permission rule. The earlier plan-review run was stopped.","timestamp":1795136518978365001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit change 3474. make verify: 1 failed, 21561 passed, then 226 integration passed. The single failure (test_repair_pause_ownership_store in_flight[doctor]) is a git update-ref exceeding the 5 s ref-lock bound while 3 verifies loaded the host. It touches no file this change edits, and the module passed 3 times in isolation. Filed as ingenious-prudish-squamata. Reproduction for this ticket: on macOS with the Windows branch forced, both goose binding tests pass.","timestamp":1795144986864121001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Main sweep evidence: test.yml run 44670297256 on main 2ca3e28fcc6a37b32b0392247b354f7681d113ed (which contains Gerrit change 3474), job 'sweep (windows)' 136069384212: 1 failed, 20304 passed, 883 skipped. Neither test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py nor any op-cert test failed. The single failure is tests/unit/test_identity_ts3_117b.py::test_off_keyring_signature_fails_enforcement. That test is not touched by this work; it fails after 9a6ed375112 ('Classify off-keyring signers apart from forgeries'), which landed between the two sweeps.","timestamp":1795152548855110001}],"created_at":1795135995058713001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"66551284-2b5a-4f25-996e-f5cc98a7de20","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"977f-11fe-1dcb-4b7d"},{"link_uuid":"3d775d78-d683-4353-85b9-e6fc7bd375cb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8eb3-f059-c663-4db3"}],"description":"## Observation\n`sweep (windows)` on main at `8c6c4f29af8` (run 44636174645, job 135955149952): 20311 passed, 1 failed. The failure is `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py::test_compose_startup_binding_fails_closed_on_bad_key` with `Failed: DID NOT RAISE OpcertKeyError`. The test passed in the earlier main sweeps.\n\n## Cause\nThe test makes the key \"too permissive\" with `chmod(0o644)` and expects the POSIX 0600 source check in `keyprov._read_path_source` to reject it. On Windows that check is skipped by design (`_POSIX_MODE_BITS`, decision cloistered-decomposed-nymph), and `chmod` cannot add group/other access. Before plump-smelly-indianabat (change 3462), the test passed on Windows only by accident: compose always failed, because `ssh-keygen` refused the OWNER RIGHTS key copy, and that raised the expected `OpcertKeyError`. Now compose succeeds on Windows, so the test's premise does not hold there.\n\n## Reproduction\nOn macOS with the Windows branch forced (`keyprov._POSIX_MODE_BITS = False`, `_restrict_dir_to_owner` a no-op), the test fails with `DID NOT RAISE OpcertKeyError`. Adding a stub that makes `_validate_key_file` raise the pre-fix OWNER RIGHTS refusal makes it pass. So the test's pass on Windows before 8c6c4f29af8 came from the copy-validation failure, not from any permission check on the source key.\n\n## Approach\nTest-only; the test is neither skipped nor deselected, and every case runs on every platform. Product behaviour is unchanged (decision cloistered-decomposed-nymph stands: no source-key permission check on Windows).\n- `test_compose_startup_binding_fails_closed_on_bad_key` keeps its name and fail-closed intent, but uses a key that is bad on every platform: a 0600 file whose content is not an OpenSSH private key. `compose_startup_opcert_binding` must raise `OpcertKeyError` (from `ssh-keygen -y` validation of the copy).\n- A new `test_compose_startup_binding_group_readable_key_follows_the_platform_rule` keeps the 0644 coverage at the binding level. It asserts `OpcertKeyError` where `keyprov._POSIX_MODE_BITS` is true. Where it is false (Windows), it asserts that compose succeeds, then calls the binding's `cleanup()`, which records the nymph decision as tested behaviour.\n- No config key, env var or flag. Portable: no platform-specific API in the test.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py` \u2014 the two tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Both tests pass on macOS (`make verify`), and on macOS with the Windows branch forced as in Reproduction.\n- After merge: a `sweep (windows)` run on main has no failures in `test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`, and both tests ran (not skipped).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `test_compose_startup_binding_fails_closed_on_bad_key` asserts `OpcertKeyError` on every platform with a key that is invalid everywhere, and a binding-level test pins the group-readable-key rule per platform (raise with POSIX mode bits, compose without).\n- [x] A `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change has no failures in `test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py","reason":"skip the POSIX-only fail-closed test on Windows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8eb3-f059-c663-4db3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"631e7dd0-6392-4362-b34e-05a9ba3bff4d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability","tests"],"ticket_id":"d8f6-2168-06e7-4133","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: goose fail-closed test relied on compose always failing; its 0644 key is not rejected on Windows by design","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c9ebddcb-09e3-41b7-bcee-d39ecceb127f","66551284-2b5a-4f25-996e-f5cc98a7de20","628b1bf7-610a-492a-b4d0-f1ecd0b91b81","7e7ca362-8660-4445-8520-e070ea8bdbcf","1928e41e-e171-4ac8-98f3-798a2fcc4a8b","e21a223e-3333-46f6-b3a7-2a448557f238","631e7dd0-6392-4362-b34e-05a9ba3bff4d","6ca0c71c-a8ac-413c-9a8b-be5358b090f7","a0c0aff4-7eb8-42a3-ae19-5de40cf7a910","3d775d78-d683-4353-85b9-e6fc7bd375cb","c71d8100-f8a6-4d7d-8c2a-826cb0e41654","8c857558-11fd-4ac5-b44c-d5ab9584132b","fba4eb91-3a6a-4bc4-b2a3-5ffa56a058cb"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795153204107015002,"uuid":"a15c9ce4-17de-4f57-bb71-1274b386221c"}
